  "comment": "wb-tz4r.5 (RI-UNIFIED-DECISION-INFERENCE-R5): the judged set of test/workbench-ri-observation-authority-census.test.ts. The three spellings of acceptance (a)'s grep are written as placeholders and composed at runtime from their words; each sha256 is the digest of the alternative's own text in the bead (the third one's dot as the plain dot), so the words cannot drift. Producer facts (read-only git show, 2026-10-23): ReactiveInferenceSDK 485f3615db1e 01-contracts.md:20 (the observation-authority sentence), 02-implementation.md:9/:21/:23 (RI-DEC-04, RI-DEC-10, initial restricted seed only), 03-conformance.md:14, the typed decision package's preflight.py:1-3 and contracts.py:55-56 (observations and typed effect policies are later slices; the package name is a sibling census's guarded spelling and is not written here); re-probed at RI origin/master 075ac589d64d: the same sentence at contracts.py:63, no observation-port or tool type, gate closed. ReactiveAgentsSDK: no checkout on the cutting host, not probed. Installed rf 0.1.836 (commit b3494ab13397): 79 leaves, the inference group's one leaf served_reachable, store_required and attach_required, its help sending a recorded render to a model and offering tool schemas from a file; no decision leaf. Pi at c6369e0: the bead's raw grep reads 3, each a leaf-path string in a captured rf leaf catalog (the knownCatalogs), 0 at the filing (trunk 1443ffb and f331270). Witnesses are what each pin's case returns on the cut's tree. wb-roxk (the R694 follow-up of landing 319) adds C1's environment shapes, C2's computed-load and wrapped-launch shapes, C3's quiet controls and three residual rows (R-ALIASED-LOADER, R-VARIABLE-COMMAND, R-EVALUATED-ENV), the outside anchor's test, the wiring constants and each pin's reached assertion count; every line above the row B label stays in place (the sibling seed-claim census pins it by line). wb-1f2w (the R694 follow-up of landing 411) adds C1's runtime-load and re-export environment shapes, C2's indirect-loader and launcher-name shapes, C3's three quiet controls and three residual rows (R-EVALUATED-LOAD, R-INDIRECT-LOADER, R-PASSED-LAUNCHER), and one assertion to every pin's reached count (the echo guard each pin's runner applies), with every line above the row B label in place. wb-tnig (the R694 follow-up of landing 509) adds C1's built-in-loader and loader-member environment shapes, C2's computed built-in load, quoted-key loader-method and launcher-alternative shapes, C3's two quiet controls and one residual row (R-COMPUTED-LAUNCHER), and one assertion to every pin's reached count (the identity reading each pin's runner applies after its case runs), with every line above the row B label in place. wb-6njq (the R694 follow-up of landing 595) adds C1's awaited process-load shape, C2's binding-default, parameter-default and await shapes, and C3's four quiet controls (otherDefaults, and R-PASSED-LAUNCHER's passedArgument, awaitedReturn and assignedDefault members), and no assertion to any pin's reached count (the identity reading's new refusal rides its one assertion; the frozen roster and the const bindings are judged-set readings), with every line above the row B label in place. wb-w0a4 (the R694 follow-up of landing 681) adds C2's import-equals and computed-literal-key launcher shapes and C3's three quiet controls (otherKeys, and R-COMPUTED-LAUNCHER's variableKey and R-PASSED-LAUNCHER's namespaceAlias members), and no assertion to any pin's reached count (the identity reading's roster-wide and plain-data refusals ride its one assertion), with every line above the row B label in place.",
